# Collapse agent identities onto the human maintainer.
#
# A `Co-authored-by` trailer naming an agent is parsed by GitHub as a
# contribution, which is how an AI agent came to appear in this repository's
# contributors graph. `.mailmap` is the belt to the commit-msg hook's braces: it
# rewrites the identity in the commit itself, so even a trailer that arrives by
# merge or by someone who never installed the hook is attributed to the person
# who actually wrote the work.
#
# Removing the trailer with a history rewrite fixed the two commits that were
# already published. These lines stop it being counted again if one returns.
#
# Only agent identities are listed. Mapping a real collaborator here would steal
# their credit, which is the opposite of what this file is for.
